{"name":"Subway","hex":"#87857c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"subway","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An underground railway, especially for mass transit of people in urban areas.","A train that runs on such an underground railway."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel by underground railway."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rapid transit","blocks":[{"text":"Rapid transit, mass rapid transit (MRT) or rail rapid transit (RRT) and commonly referred to as metro, is a type of high-capacity public transport that is generally built in urban areas. A grade separated rapid transit line below ground surface through a tunnel can be regionally called a subway, tube, metro or underground. They are sometimes grade-separated on elevated railways, in which case some are referred to as elevated, el or L trains – short for \"elevated\" – or skytrains. A common alternative term for rapid transit in North America is heavy rail. Rapid transit systems are usually electric railways that, unlike buses or trams, operate on an exclusive right-of-way, which cannot be accessed by pedestrians or other vehicles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Seoul-metro-2009-20180916-103548.jpg/330px-Seoul-metro-2009-20180916-103548.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapid_transit","wikidata":"Q5503"},{"title":"Subway (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"Subway IP LLC, trading as Subway, is an American multinational fast food restaurant franchise that specializes in submarine sandwiches (subs) and wraps. It was founded by Fred DeLuca and financed by Peter Buck in 1965 as Pete's Super Submarine Sandwiches in Bridgeport, Connecticut. After several name changes, it was renamed Subway in 1972, and a franchise operation began in 1974 with a second restaurant in Wallingford, Connecticut."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/A_Subway_restaurant_in_a_strip_mall_in_Franklin%2C_North_Carolina%2C_United_States.jpg/330px-A_Subway_restaurant_in_a_strip_mall_in_Franklin%2C_North_Carolina%2C_United_States.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subway_(restaurant)","wikidata":"Q244457"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/R211_A_train_approaching_80th_Street_August_2025.jpg/500px-R211_A_train_approaching_80th_Street_August_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/R211_A_train_approaching_80th_Street_August_2025.jpg/1280px-R211_A_train_approaching_80th_Street_August_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/R211_A_train_approaching_80th_Street_August_2025.jpg/500px-R211_A_train_approaching_80th_Street_August_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AR211_A_train_approaching_80th_Street_August_2025.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/London_Underground_2024_tube_stock_approaching_Turnham_Green_during_a_test_run_%28March_2026%29_%281%29.jpg/500px-London_Underground_2024_tube_stock_approaching_Turnham_Green_during_a_test_run_%28March_2026%29_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/London_Underground_2024_tube_stock_approaching_Turnham_Green_during_a_test_run_%28March_2026%29_%281%29.jpg/1280px-London_Underground_2024_tube_stock_approaching_Turnham_Green_during_a_test_run_%28March_2026%29_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c